[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_imo08")
dialogue_id = "mq_4_40_teo_diary"
record_title = "Era 四: The Oldest Texts"
text = "PAGE: avatar_adult(MUSEUM_SECONDARY), historian(MUSEUM_PRIMARY)
historian: Oh, that's a rare sight!
historian: Welcome to my humble museum.
historian: What brings you here today?
avatar_adult: I have something for you.
avatar_adult: I was hoping you could help me.
historian: Are those... the commandment scrolls?
historian: The Scribe has always been too protective to let me handle these before.
historian: But... he knows better than to try to bribe me, even if it [i]is[/i] a priceless treasure.
avatar_adult: Well, actually...
avatar_adult: He doesn't know I was bringing them to you.
historian: Oh?
historian: Well, that's a delightful surprise.
avatar_adult: Anyway, you can translate these, right?
historian: I would be thrilled!
historian: But I must temper your expectations.
historian: These ancient records rarely give us neat answers.
historian: They might just raise more questions.
historian: Or end up being unrelated entirely.
historian: Are you sure you are ready for that?
avatar_adult: Whatever the truth is, I want to hear it.
avatar_adult: I have stared at those scrolls my whole life and felt nothing.
avatar_adult: Maybe if I hear them in a language I understand, it would finally spark my memory.
historian: The mind is a vast room, but sometimes all it takes is a candle to illuminate it.
historian: I can't promise it will be the spark you are looking for, but I will do my best to not let my opinion color the translation.
avatar_adult: Thank you, Historian.
avatar_adult: That's all I ask.
historian: You know, I had assumed you were content being a symbol on the Scribe's banner.
historian: I'm glad to learn you are a fellow seeker of truth."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://jtkfcsyiryo4"
